  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nFind the value of: frac{{3sqrt 2 }}{{sqrt 6 - sqrt 3 }} - frac{{4sqrt 3 }}{{sqrt 6 - sqrt 2 }} - (6)/({sqrt 8 {{ - )}sqrt {12} }}{{}}\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nRationalize the denominator using the formula: a / (b + c) = a(b - c) / (b² - c²).\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nFirst term: (3√2 / (√6 - √3))\n\n⇒ Rationalize: (3√2 × (√6 + √3)) / ((√6 + √3)(√6 - √3))\n\n⇒ (3√2(√6 + √3)) / (6 - 3) = √2(√6 + √3)\n\n⇒ √12 + √6 = 2√3 + √6\n\nSecond term: (4√3 / (√6 - √2))\n\n⇒ Rationalize: (4√3 × (√6 + √2)) / ((√6 + √2)(√6 - √2))\n\n⇒ (4√3(√6 + √2)) / (6 - 2) = √3(√6 + √2)\n\n⇒ √18 + √6 = 3√2 + √6\n\nThird term: (6 / (√8 - √12))\n\n⇒ Rationalize: (6 × (√8 + √12)) / ((√8 - √12)(√8 + √12))\n\n⇒ (6(√8 + √12)) / (8 - 12) = -(6(√8 + √12)) / 4 = -(3/2)(√8 + √12)\n\n⇒ -(3/2)(2√2 + 2√3) = -3(√2 + √3)\n\n**Final Calculation:**\n\n2√3 + √6 - (3√2 + √6) - (-3(√2 + √3))\n\n2√3 + √6 - 3√2 - √6 + 3√2 + 3√3\n\n⇒ 5√3 + 0 + 0\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 5√3.**",
